<article class="env-lemma" id="0EU2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EU2">Lemma <span data-tag="0EU2">38.34.14</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\mathit{Sch}_ h$ be a big h site containing $S$. Then $(\textit{Aff}/S)_ h$ is a site. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Reasoning as in the proof of Topologies, Lemma <a href="/tag/021C" data-tag="021C">34.4.9</a> it suffices to show that the collection of standard h coverings satisfies properties (1), (2) and (3) of Sites, Definition <a href="/tag/00VH" data-tag="00VH">7.6.2</a>. This is clear since for example, given a standard h covering $\{ T_ i \to T\} _{i\in I}$ and for each $i$ a standard h covering $\{ T_{ij} \to T_ i\} _{j \in J_ i}$, then $\{ T_{ij} \to T\} _{i \in I, j\in J_ i}$ is a h covering (Lemma <a href="/tag/0ETY" data-tag="0ETY">38.34.9</a>), $\bigcup _{i\in I} J_ i$ is finite and each $T_{ij}$ is affine. Thus $\{ T_{ij} \to T\} _{i \in I, j\in J_ i}$ is a standard h covering. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>